---
description: This rule provides a command to automatically identify and fix common linting and compilation issues in a specified module, and verify the fixes are successful.
alwaysApply: false
---
## arguments
## arguments
## arguments
## arguments
## arguments
- moduleName: The name of the module to fix (e.g., course-service, ui-components, DoorSync-core, learn, shell, main.scss)
- taskDescription: Description of the fix task  default value: Fix linting and compilation issues in {{moduleName}} module
- taskId: The ID of the task to update (will be set after task creation)

## init
1. **Create task for tracking fixes**
   - Use @create-task.mdc directly with:
     - title: "Fix issues in {{moduleName}} module"
     - description: "{{taskDescription}}"
     - assignee: (current user)
     - priority: "Medium"
     - type: "Maintenance"
     - component: "DevOps"
   - Note the created task ID and store it in the taskId variable
   - IMPORTANT: The task creation MUST be completed before proceeding

2. Determine module type and path based on provided name:
   - Backend service (Java) - in `/apis` directory:
     - task-service: `/apis/task-service`
     - course-service: `/apis/course-service`
     - event-service: `/apis/event-service`
     - company-service: `/apis/company-service`
     - reference-service: `/apis/reference-service`
     - audit-service: `/apis/audit-service`
     - author-service: `/apis/author-service`
     - batch-service: `/apis/batch-service`
     - test-service: `/apis/test-service`
     - learner-service: `/apis/learner-service`
     - metadata-service: `/apis/metadata-service`
     - communication-service: `/apis/communication-service`
     - caching-service: `/apis/caching-service`
     - rewards-service: `/apis/rewards-service`
     - platform-admin-service: `/apis/platform-admin-service`
     - iam-service: `/apis/iam-service`
     - document-service: `/apis/document-service`
     - user-service: `/apis/user-service`
     - DoorSync-core: `/libs/DoorSync-core`
     - Builder: Maven (`mvn`)

   - Frontend feature app - in `/apps` directory:
     - shell: `/apps/shell`
     - admin: `/apps/admin`
     - onboard: `/apps/onboard`
     - hire: `/apps/hire`
     - learn: `/apps/learn`
     - auth: `/apps/auth`
     - Builder: Nx with Angular (`npx nx`)

   - Libraries - in `/libs` directory:
     - ui-components: `/libs/ui-components`
     - DoorSync-core: `/libs/DoorSync-core`
     - shared-utils: `/libs/shared-utils`
     - data-access: `/libs/data-access`
     - Builder: Nx with Angular (`npx nx`)

   - SCSS styling - in `/styles` directory:
     - main.scss: `/styles/main.scss`
     - Builder: SASS compiler (`sass`)

3. Identify appropriate linting and build tools based on module type:
   - Java: Maven, Checkstyle, PMD, SpotBugs
   - Angular: ESLint via Nx, Prettier
   - SCSS: Stylelint, SASS compiler

4. Validate that the module exists in the workspace
5. Use @update-task-journal.mdc with:
   - taskId: {{taskId}}
   - entry: "Identified module type and appropriate tools for {{moduleName}}"

## perform
1. **Identify issues**
   - For Java modules (backend services):
     - Run `mvn validate -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml` to check for Maven configuration issues
     - Run `mvn compile -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml` for compilation errors
     - Run `mvn checkstyle:check -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml` for code style issues
     - Run `mvn pmd:check -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml` for code quality issues
   - For Angular/Frontend modules:
     - For apps: Run `npx nx lint {{moduleName}}` to identify TypeScript/HTML linting issues
     - For libs: Run `npx nx lint {{moduleName}}` to identify TypeScript/HTML linting issues
     - For apps: Run `npx nx build {{moduleName}} --configuration=development` to check for compile errors
     - For libs: Run `npx nx build {{moduleName}}` to check for compile errors
   - For SCSS files:
     - Run `npx stylelint "styles/{{moduleName}}/**/*.scss"` to check for SCSS linting issues
     - For main.scss: Run `sass styles/main.scss styles/compiled/main.css` to verify compilation success
     - For other styles: Run `sass styles/{{moduleName}}/_index.scss styles/compiled/{{moduleName}}.css` to verify compilation success
   - Use @update-task-journal.mdc with:
     - taskId: {{taskId}}
     - entry: "Identified issues in {{moduleName}} module"
     - subtaskIndex: 1
     - subtaskStatus: "Completed"

2. **Apply automated fixes**
   - For Java modules:
     - Run `mvn formatter:format -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml` to auto-format code
     - Run `mvn imports:fix -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml` to organize imports
     - Run Maven dependency plugin to fix dependency issues if detected
   - For Angular/Frontend modules:
     - For apps: Run `npx nx lint {{moduleName}} --fix` to automatically fix linting issues
     - For libs: Run `npx nx lint {{moduleName}} --fix` to automatically fix linting issues
     - For apps: Run `npx prettier --write "apps/{{moduleName}}/src/**/*.{ts,html,scss}"` for formatting
     - For libs: Run `npx prettier --write "libs/{{moduleName}}/src/**/*.{ts,html,scss}"` for formatting
   - For SCSS files:
     - Run `npx stylelint "styles/{{moduleName}}/**/*.scss" --fix` to automatically fix styling issues
     - Fix common SASS compilation errors (missing variables, syntax errors)
   - Use @update-task-journal.mdc with:
     - taskId: {{taskId}}
     - entry: "Applied automated fixes to {{moduleName}} module"
     - subtaskIndex: 2
     - subtaskStatus: "Completed"

3. **Check and fix Angular component architecture issues**
   - Check for component standalone property mismatches with modules:
     - Run `grep -r "standalone: true" apps/{{moduleName}}/src` to find standalone components
     - For components declared in NgModules, ensure they aren't marked as standalone
     - For standalone components, ensure they aren't declared in NgModules
   - Check for empty constructors and unused imports:
     - Fix empty constructors by removing them
     - Fix unused imports by removing them
   - Use @update-task-journal.mdc with:
     - taskId: {{taskId}}
     - entry: "Fixed component architecture issues in {{moduleName}} module"
     - subtaskIndex: 3
     - subtaskStatus: "Completed"

4. **Generate report of identified issues and applied fixes**
   - Create a summary of:
     - Total issues found
     - Issues automatically fixed
     - Issues requiring manual intervention
   - For each issue requiring manual intervention:
     - File path and line number
     - Issue description
     - Suggested fix approach
   - Use @update-task-journal.mdc with:
     - taskId: {{taskId}}
     - entry: "Generated report of issues and fixes for {{moduleName}} module"
     - subtaskIndex: 4
     - subtaskStatus: "Completed"

5. **Verify fixes**
   - Rerun linting/compilation tools to confirm issues are resolved:
     - Java: `mvn verify -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml`
     - Angular apps: `npx nx build {{moduleName}} --configuration=development`
     - Angular libs: `npx nx build {{moduleName}}`
     - SCSS main: `sass styles/main.scss styles/compiled/main.css`
     - SCSS modules: `sass styles/{{moduleName}}/_index.scss styles/compiled/{{moduleName}}.css`
   - If new issues appear, attempt additional automated fixes
   - Identify any remaining issues that require manual intervention
   - Use @update-task-journal.mdc with:
     - taskId: {{taskId}}
     - entry: "Verified fixes in {{moduleName}} module"
     - subtaskIndex: 5
     - subtaskStatus: "Completed"

## finalize
1. Confirm successful fixes with summary statistics
2. Recompile or rebuild to verify everything works:
   - Java: `mvn clean install -f /apis/{{moduleName}}/pom.xml`
   - Angular apps: `npx nx build {{moduleName}} --configuration=production`
   - Angular libs: `npx nx build {{moduleName}} --configuration=production`
   - SCSS main: `sass styles/main.scss styles/compiled/main.css --style=compressed`
   - SCSS modules: `sass styles/{{moduleName}}/_index.scss styles/compiled/{{moduleName}}.css --style=compressed`
3. Provide detailed report of what was fixed and what still needs attention
4. Suggest next steps (e.g., "Run tests to ensure fixes don't introduce regressions")
5. For Angular projects, note any remaining TypeScript warnings about unused files
6. Use @update-task-journal.mdc with:
   - taskId: {{taskId}}
   - entry: "Completed fixing issues in {{moduleName}} module"

7. **Complete the fix task**
   - Use @complete-task.mdc directly with:
     - taskId: {{taskId}}
   - This will mark the task as completed and move it to the completed tasks directory
   - Ensure this step is ALWAYS executed to properly close the task
